# NIMBUS environment configuration
# Copy this file to ".env" and adjust values as needed.
# Never commit the real ".env" file — it is gitignored.

# Logging verbosity: error | warn | info | debug
NIMBUS_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Application environment: development | production
NIMBUS_ENV=development

# --- Weather ---
# NIMBUS's weather provider (Open-Meteo) is free and requires no API key.
# Location is automatic (IP-based) by default. To use a fixed location
# instead — without going through the Settings UI — set the location mode
# to "manual" in Settings and provide these as a default/fallback, or set
# them here for headless/dev use:
# NIMBUS_WEATHER_LAT=38.7223
# NIMBUS_WEATHER_LON=-9.1393
# NIMBUS_WEATHER_LOCATION_LABEL=Lisbon, Portugal

# --- Calendar ---
# NIMBUS's calendar provider reads an ICS ("iCalendar") feed — no OAuth,
# no API key. Most calendar apps (Google Calendar, Outlook, iCloud) can
# generate a private "secret address in iCal format" for a calendar under
# their sharing/settings page. Treat this URL like a password: never
# commit it, never share it.
#
# Calendar awareness must still be enabled in Settings (it's off by
# default). These env vars only supply a *default* feed for headless/dev
# use, when calendar is enabled but no feed has been saved yet — normal
# use is to add a feed from the Settings tab instead.
# NIMBUS_CALENDAR_ICS_URL=https://calendar.example.com/private-xyz/basic.ics
# NIMBUS_CALENDAR_LABEL=Personal

# --- Email ---
# NIMBUS's email provider connects over IMAP (read-only) — no OAuth app
# registration needed. Most providers (Gmail, Outlook, iCloud) require an
# app-specific password rather than your normal account password; generate
# one from the provider's account security settings. Treat it like any
# other credential: never commit it, never share it.
#
# Email awareness must still be enabled in Settings (it's off by default).
# These env vars only supply a *default* account for headless/dev use, when
# email is enabled but no account has been saved yet — normal use is to
# add an account from the Settings tab instead.
# NIMBUS_EMAIL_HOST=imap.gmail.com
# NIMBUS_EMAIL_PORT=993
# NIMBUS_EMAIL_SECURE=true
# NIMBUS_EMAIL_USERNAME=you@example.com
# NIMBUS_EMAIL_PASSWORD=app-specific-password
# NIMBUS_EMAIL_LABEL=Personal

# --- Tasks ---
# NIMBUS's task provider connects to Todoist's REST API using a personal
# API token — no OAuth app registration needed. Generate one from Todoist
# Settings > Integrations > Developer. Treat it like any other credential:
# never commit it, never share it.
#
# Task awareness must still be enabled in Settings (it's off by default).
# This env var only supplies a *default* account for headless/dev use, when
# tasks are enabled but no account has been saved yet — normal use is to
# add an account from the Settings tab instead.
# NIMBUS_TASKS_TODOIST_TOKEN=your-personal-api-token
# NIMBUS_TASKS_LABEL=Personal

# --- Spotify ---
# NIMBUS controls Spotify via its Web API, authenticated with the
# Authorization Code + PKCE flow — this needs a Client ID from your own
# free Spotify Developer app (https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard),
# but never a client secret (PKCE doesn't use one). Create an app there,
# then add this exact Redirect URI to it (the port must match
# NIMBUS_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_PORT below, default 8888):
#   http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback
#
# Spotify control must still be enabled in Settings (it's off by
# default), and connecting your account happens from the Settings tab's
# "Connect" button (opens your browser for Spotify's normal sign-in) —
# NIMBUS never sees your Spotify password. The Client ID itself isn't a
# secret, but is still kept out of source since a shared NIMBUS-wide app
# would collide across installs — see docs/spotify.md.
# NIMBUS_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=your-spotify-app-client-id
# NIMBUS_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_PORT=8888
